WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.675
So what actually has to move?

2
00:00:01.675 --> 00:00:04.275
Two points drive everything
in this session.

3
00:00:04.275 --> 00:00:06.887
First, placement becomes attributes.

4
00:00:06.887 --> 00:00:10.101
In Active Directory, where
an object sits in the OU

5
00:00:10.101 --> 00:00:13.550
tree decides who manages it
and which policy applies.

6
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.375
Entra ID has no tree.

7
00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:20.187
It governs objects by what they carry:
attributes, memberships and roles.

8
00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:22.917
Administrative units
help, but they can't nest,

9
00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:27.225
and for synced users the attribute
values are still written on-premises.

10
00:00:27.225 --> 00:00:30.650
Second, the surface is bigger
than users and groups.

11
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:36.137
The program's inventory names eleven
dependency types, and some, like PKI,

12
00:00:36.137 --> 00:00:41.350
RADIUS and LDAP-bound applications,
fail silently when AD goes away.

13
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.712
Each dependency gets an adapter,
and the sync engine finishes last.

14
00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:50.380
The rest of this session is how you find
all of that, rebuild it, and prove it.
